# The ending illustration (Scene phase, D-107): 288x120, drawn at 16,12 on
# navy B. A 4 px Biedermeier picture frame (gold Y/o/O, bead moulding,
# square corner blocks). Inside, Cafe Zauner: cream c wall under an o
# egg-and-dart cornice, G/j wainscoting, w/i marble chequer floor. Resi (her
# player look, seated, from the side, a fork in her hand) on a bentwood l/O
# Thonet chair at a marble table (w/i top, d/m pedestal); on it the
# Zaunerstollen on a w/i plate and a silver tray with a Melange (w/c foam,
# O crema) and a glass of water s/h. The Oberkellner bows beside the table
# (tails d/k, w shirt, d pomaded head with an i shine, n moustache, napkin
# w/i over his forearm). Through the G/j window the Pfarrgasse: pastel
# houses, the Stadtpfarrkirche spire t/T, the queue (the warteschlange
# figures, upper bodies above the sill) and Postbus 150 driving past, full
# (the postbus halt faces, drive hubs). Left: a gold-framed Katrin painting,
# newspapers on wooden holders; right: Oblaten tins, Stollen boxes and
# Gugelhupfe on shelves over the counter and its cake vitrine. No text.
# idle 2f/20t: the Melange's steam wisps change, the man in Lederhosen in
# the queue checks his phone, the bus's hubs turn.
# Drawn by the pixel-artist with a throwaway script; the grid below is the
# source.
sprite = ending_cafe
size   = 288x120
origin = 0,0
anim   = idle frames=2 ticks=20 loop
